{
  "id": "proofs.parity.sum-of-evens",
  "course": "proofs",
  "topic": "parity",
  "kind": "parity_proof",
  "title": "The sum of two even integers",
  "prompt": "Prove: if $m$ and $n$ are even integers, then $m + n$ is even.",
  "answer_format": "A structured proof: let, case, expr and witness steps (notes optional). No final answer box.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "tags": [
    "direct proof",
    "parity"
  ],
  "data": {
    "variables": [
      "m",
      "n"
    ],
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "var": "m",
        "is": "even"
      },
      {
        "var": "n",
        "is": "even"
      }
    ],
    "target": "m + n",
    "goal": "even"
  },
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Write m and n using the definition of even. Do they have to be twice the same integer?",
    "Factor a 2 out of m + n."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $m$ and $n$ are even, $m = 2j$ and $n = 2k$ for some integers $j$ and $k$.",
    "Then $m + n = 2j + 2k = 2(j + k)$, and $j + k$ is an integer, so $m + n$ is even. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "sundstrom-mr3",
    "section": "1.2 Constructing Direct Proofs",
    "note": "Original problem."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "retired",
    "notes": "Invented problem, retired 2026-11-06: MATH 123 proofs now map 1:1 to Book of Proof exercises."
  },
